# ZyperOS's init (/etc/init.d/zyperos) on the GKD Pixel 2, read only when it
# copies ZyperOS onto the card (a new card's first start, or the first start
# of a newer system image).
#
# The CPU's ceiling while it copies, in kHz. Rockchip's own firmware for this
# chip (the stock system's device tree, and twigUI's, under bus-apll) raises
# vdd_logic, the supply of the DDR controller, the buses and the GPU, to
# 1.0 V whenever the CPU's PLL runs above 1008 MHz, and lets it down to
# 0.95 V only at 1008 or below. plastron's kernel has nothing that does
# that: vdd_logic is what the DDR and the GPU ask for, which with the GPU
# idle, as it is under the boot animation, can be 0.95 V. The copy runs
# before rcS, under the kernel's performance governor, so without a ceiling
# the CPU would spend it all at 1296 MHz, outside what Rockchip runs at that
# voltage, while the card and the DDR are at their busiest. At 1008 the
# copy is inside it, and barely slower: it waits on the card, not the CPU.
SETUP_CPU_MAX=1008000
